<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<main id="main">
  <section class="pageHero compact"><div class="container"><span class="kicker">Service information</span><h1>Delivery & Provisioning Policy</h1><p>How VPN4U confirms, provisions and delivers hosting and VPN services.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container legalProse">
    <h2>1. Order review</h2>
    <p>VPN4U uses a confirmation-first ordering process. Submitting an order request does not itself take payment or guarantee that a particular configuration is available. We review stock, region, capacity and material configuration details before accepting the order.</p>

    <h2>2. Confirmation before payment</h2>
    <p>Where the requested service is available, VPN4U confirms the material specification and final price before payment is requested. If a requested dedicated-server model or regional resource is unavailable, we may offer an alternative or ask whether you prefer to wait.</p>

    <h2>3. VPS provisioning</h2>
    <p>Standard VPS services are usually provisioned within one business day after order approval and any required payment. Provisioning can take longer where manual review, a non-standard image, regional capacity or additional network resources are required.</p>

    <h2>4. Dedicated-server provisioning</h2>
    <p>Dedicated servers are physical inventory and are typically provisioned within 1–3 business days after approval, subject to stock, datacentre location, hardware preparation and any custom configuration. Non-standard hardware or software requirements can take longer.</p>

    <h2>5. VPN activation</h2>
    <p>Standard VPN access is usually activated within one business day after order approval and any required payment. Device and protocol information is supplied for the accepted plan.</p>

    <h2>6. How access is delivered</h2>
    <p>Provisioning notices and access information are sent using the contact details associated with the order. Customers are responsible for ensuring that the supplied email address is accurate and monitored.</p>

    <h2>7. Delivery estimates</h2>
    <p>Website delivery times are estimates rather than guaranteed deadlines unless a written service-level or delivery commitment is explicitly included in the accepted order. Upstream maintenance, hardware stock, security review, licensing and custom work can affect delivery time.</p>

    <h2>8. Failed or delayed provisioning</h2>
    <p>If provisioning is materially delayed, VPN4U will try to provide an updated estimate or an alternative where appropriate. If VPN4U is unable to deliver an accepted service, applicable remedies are handled under the Cancellation & Refund Policy and applicable law.</p>

    <h2>9. Customer action required</h2>
    <p>Provisioning may be delayed where we are waiting for required customer information, identity or fraud checks, technical clarification, acceptance of a revised specification or another action reasonably necessary to supply the service.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about an order or provisioning status can be sent to <a href="mailto:<%= site.emails.support %>"><%= site.emails.support %></a>. Pre-sales configuration questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:<%= site.emails.sales %>"><%= site.emails.sales %></a>.</p>
  </div></section>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
